            "content": "== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|Description = Soprano [[Montserrat Alavedra i Comas]] is joined by [[William McColl]], clarinet, and [[Joseph Levine]], fortepiano. The clarinet is a Bb clarinet made by Mollenhauer in [[Fulda, Germany]] about 1820 - 1825. The [[fortepiano]] was a copy of a Mozart-era instrument.\n|Source = The Al Goldstein collection in the [http://music.ibiblio.org/pub/multimedia/pandora/vorbis/index.html Pandora Music] repository at ibiblio.org.\n|Date = \n|Author =[[Giacomo Meyerbeer]]\n|Permission = The [http://music.ibiblio.org/pub/multimedia/pandora/vorbis/Read.html license information] states that this file is \"available for free download subject to the [[EFF OAL]]\" (Open Audio License), which in turn [https://www.eff.org/IP/Open_licenses/eff_oal.php is interchangeable] with the [[CC-BY-SA-2.0]].\n}}\n== {{int:license-header}} ==\n{{cc-by-sa-2.0}}\n\n[[Category:Compositions by Giacomo Meyerbeer|Hirtenlied]]\n[[Category:Montserrat Alavedra]]\n[[Category:Audio files of Romantic period classical music]]\n[[Category:Audio files of sopranos singing]]\n[[Category:Fortepiano music]]\n[[Category:Pandora Music]]",
